WEBVTT

00:00:00.315 --> 00:00:03.997
Now minimize the fictional input. Keep only the

00:00:04.042 --> 00:00:07.680
order-delay issue and the supplied training policy. Remove

00:00:07.769 --> 00:00:11.812
contact details, the family circumstance and unnecessary order

00:00:11.992 --> 00:00:15.260
identifiers. Replace the customer with a fictional role.

00:00:15.431 --> 00:00:18.349
The policy says acknowledge the issue and ask

00:00:18.529 --> 00:00:21.628
authorized support to verify status before promising a

00:00:21.674 --> 00:00:25.131
delivery date. No date has been confirmed. Ask

00:00:25.221 --> 00:00:28.024
AI to draft only an acknowledgment. Review the

00:00:28.069 --> 00:00:31.123
result for invented tracking information or an unsupported

00:00:31.213 --> 00:00:34.581
promise. Save the safer input and explain one

00:00:34.672 --> 00:00:37.905
removal. This draft is practice; it is not

00:00:37.951 --> 00:00:40.016
a sent customer message or proof that a

00:00:40.061 --> 00:00:41.300
real account is approved.
